    "narrative": "Our lineup for July 25th centers on an aggressive targeting of RHP Ryan Johnson and RHP Bryce Elder, both of whom present prime opportunities for our offense. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** leads the charge with a 73.70 efficiency score, buoyed by a favorable matchup against Nick Martinez and his 4.91 xERA. Joining him in the elite tier are **Lawrence Butler** (68.68) and **Dylan Beavers** (68.38), both of whom benefit significantly from the +16% park factor and the positive wind trajectory against Elder. **Luis Arraez** (66.78) and **Jung Hoo Lee** (65.48) round out our high-efficiency anchors; their ability to leverage the +19% SP skill advantage against Johnson makes them pivotal for accumulating AVG and R while maintaining roster efficiency.\n\nOur primary platoon and park-adjusted edges are concentrated in the outfield and middle infield, where the combination of favorable park factors and high-velocity matchup targets is most pronounced. **Taylor Ward** stands out with an impressive 63.35 score, largely driven by a massive +16% park boost against Elder. While **Jonathan Aranda** is slated for a solid outing (65.77) against Bibee, we are monitoring the risks associated with his specific park and platoon splits. The most difficult decision today involved the bench; **Drew Gilbert** was our closest exclusion at 55.03. While **Drew Gilbert** benefited from the same wind-aided environment as **Luis Arraez**, the superior raw projections of our active starters forced him to the pine to preserve game caps. We are also proceeding with caution regarding **Yainer Diaz** (44.38) and **Cal Raleigh** (47.09); despite their importance, their scores are dampened by elite SP skill metrics from Burke and Eovaldi, suggesting a game script where efficiency will be harder to come by behind the dish.",
